PCRE.NET LICENCE\par
----------------\par
\par
PCRE.NET is a .NET library which wraps and includes PCRE2. It is distributed\par
under the terms of the same "BSD" licence as PCRE2, as specified below.\par
\par
\par
PCRE2 LICENCE\par
-------------\par
\par
PCRE2 is a library of functions to support regular expressions whose syntax\par
and semantics are as close as possible to those of the Perl 5 language.\par
\par
Releases 10.00 and above of PCRE2 are distributed under the terms of the "BSD"\par
licence, as specified below, with one exemption for certain binary\par
redistributions. The documentation for PCRE2, supplied in the "doc" directory,\par
is distributed under the same terms as the software itself. The data in the\par
testdata directory is not copyrighted and is in the public domain.\par
\par
The basic library functions are written in C and are freestanding. Also\par
included in the distribution is a just-in-time compiler that can be used to\par
optimize pattern matching. This is an optional feature that can be omitted when\par
the library is built.\par
